OMP development assets

Source: https://github.com/can1357/oh-my-pi
Snapshot commit: 5d0aaffaf1f987503ce129a642fb6e30339615af
License: MIT (see LICENSE)

Copied paths:
- .omp/commands/ -> commands/
- .omp/skills/ -> skills/
- .omp/tools/tui.ts -> tools/tui.ts

Packaging adaptations:
- Declare tui.ts runtime dependencies at the agent-plugins package root.
- Point tui.ts missing-dependency errors at both linked-checkout and installed-package recovery.
- Resolve lazy TUI dependencies from the packaged tool directory so compiled OMP can load linked or installed dependencies.
- Launch TypeScript file targets with bun from PATH because compiled OMP exposes its own binary as process.execPath.
- Retain the node:net debug-socket client so the tool loads on OMP 18.9.x; upstream's IpcConnection client requires OMP 18.10 or newer.
- Pin commands that can write remotely to clssck/oh-my-pi and forbid writes to can1357/oh-my-pi.
- Remove retired IRC references from the builtin prompt probe so it loads against current OMP tool exports.
- Resolve prompt-probe runtime modules from the caller's OMP checkout and run the packaged entry points through `skill://` paths.

This is a reviewed snapshot, not an automatic mirror. `omp-source-lock.json` records upstream Git object hashes for the copied assets plus the OMP docs and source files that define their loading contracts; CI opens or updates an assigned issue when any recorded object changes upstream.
